{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When you enter</b> Written above this: <b>you shall blot out the memory of Amalek</b>, and juxtaposed to it: <b>And it shall be, when you enter the land</b> — that they were commanded to blot out the memory of Amalek immediately upon their entry into the land, because he sought to prevent their entry into the land, for he told the king of Egypt that the people had fled. And likewise he told Laban that Jacob had fled. Therefore the portion of firstfruits, in which is mentioned <b>Aramean sought to destroy my father</b>, was juxtaposed to it. כי עולה למנין ל'. תבוא. אותיות אבות. And this is what they expounded regarding the sinew of the thigh, that the redemption of Israel does not come with fewer than 30 righteous who are reckoned as the fathers:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:42.521577337Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}